# Copied from `dist/install.sh` at build time so the site can serve the
# script its own headline command pipes into a shell. Not committed: two
# copies of an install script in one repo is one copy too many, and the
# stale one is always the one somebody curls.
/public/install.sh

# Mirrored out of `packages/webfonts/dist` by vite.config.ts at build time —
# the `secreq-webfonts` crate builds into its own project, and `^build` reaches
# it from here. Not committed: the output is a pure function of a pinned crate,
# so a stored copy could only ever fall behind it. The licences are written out
# beside them for the same reason — they must cover the exact bytes shipped.
/public/fonts
